   (Acetic acid) + (Ethyl alcohol) ⇌ (Ethyl ether) + (Ethyl ester)  
   The reaction starts with 1 g-mol of acetic acid and 1 g-mole of ethyl alcohol.  
   At equilibrium, 0.333 g-moles of acetic acid remain.  

2. **Calculate the amount of acetic acid consumed**:  
   Initial moles of acetic acid = 1 g-mole  
   Moles of acetic acid at equilibrium = 0.333 g-mole  
   Moles of acetic acid consumed = 1 - 0.333 = 0.667 g-mole  

