\[
\text{Dose (J/kg)} = \frac{0.12 \text{ J}}{1.8 \text{ kg}} = 0.067 \text{ J/kg}
\]
The dose is given in J/kg, which is the equivalent dose in units of J/kg. To convert this to other units like mSv (millisieverts), we need to multiply by the radiation quality factor (RBE), which depends on the type of radiation. For therapeutic radiopharmaceuticals, the RBE is typically 1.0 for gamma rays and neutrons, and 2.0 for beta particles. For this calculation, we assume the RBE is 1.0, as the question does not specify the type of radiation.

