\[
\text{Dose (mSv)} = \text{Dose (J/kg)} \times 10^6 \text{ J/MeV} \times 1 \text{ MeV/Gy} \times 1 \text{ Gy/mSv}
\]
However, the direct conversion from J/kg to mSv is not straightforward because it depends on the type of radiation and its energy. Instead, we can express the dose in J/kg, which is a standard unit for radiation dose.

