   - Wet-bulb temperature (Tw) = 17°C = 17.0°C  

2. **Use EES to calculate the properties**:  
   - EES has built-in psychrometric properties.  
   - Create a new EES model and enter the following:  
     ```
     P = 101320;  
     T = 24;  
     Tw = 17;  

     (h, H, RH, T_dew, V) = psychrometric(P, T, Tw);  
     \n
     h = specific humidity (kg/kg air)  
     H = enthalpy (kJ/kg dry air)  

     RH = relative humidity (%)  
     T_dew = dew-point temperature (°C)  
     V = specific volume (m³/kg dry air)  
